{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"toolu_01HVrtp7Xy674bMNfqv8HAnK","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /app && cat .ki-base/decisions/0003-style-composition-and-ansi.md | head -70; echo ----; cat .ki-base/decisions/0001-terminal-segments.md | head -50; echo ----; grep -n \"__all__\\|^from\\|^import\" rich/__init__.py | head; echo ----; sed -n 1,40p rich/padding.py | head -5; ls tests | head -80"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n"}],"details":{}}}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"toolu_01HVrtp7Xy674bMNfqv8HAnK","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /app && cat .ki-base/decisions/0003-style-composition-and-ansi.md | head -70; echo ----; cat .ki-base/decisions/0001-terminal-segments.md | head -50; echo ----; grep -n \"__all__\\|^from\\|^import\" rich/__init__.py | head; echo ----; sed -n 1,40p rich/padding.py | head -5; ls tests | head -80"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n----\n# ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nTerminal emulators operate on streams of characters interspersed with ANSI escape codes for styling and cursor movement. Without a unified primitive abstraction, high-level components (tables, syntax, markdown) would have to manually track escape codes, calculate visual cell widths, and handle cross-platform line breaks, leading to exponential complexity and bugs.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Atomic Segment Primitive:**  \n   Every visual element in Rich must ultimately reduce to a stream of `Segment` instances:\n   ```python\n   class Segment(NamedTuple):\n       text: str\n       style: Optional[Style] = None\n       control: Optional[Sequence[ControlCode]] = None\n   ```\n2. **Strict Invariants:**\n   - A `Segment` text piece must not contain unescaped newline characters `\\n` or `\\r` unless processed by `Segment.split_lines()` or `Segment.split_and_crop_lines()`.\n   - Visual measurement is derived strictly from `cell_len(segment.text)` using East Asian Width Unicode tables, never raw `len(text)`.\n   - Control sequences (cursor up, color palette queries) are encapsulated in the optional `control` field and take zero visual cell length.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- All rendering operations are stateless stream-processing pipelines.\n- Layout algorithms only need to measure and slice `Segment` collections.\n- Clean separation between logical layout calculation and physical terminal escape emission.\n----\n3:import os\n4:from typing import IO, TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable, Optional, Union\n6:from ._extension import load_ipython_extension  # noqa: F401\n8:__all__ = [\"get_console\", \"reconfigure\", \"print\", \"inspect\", \"print_json\"]\n----\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, List, Optional, Tuple, Union\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import (\n        Console,\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\n_card_render.py\nconftest.py\npytest.ini\nrender.py\ntest_align.py\ntest_ansi.py\ntest_bar.py\ntest_block_bar.py\ntest_box.py\ntest_card.py\ntest_cells.py\ntest_color.py\ntest_color_triplet.py\ntest_columns.py\ntest_columns_align.py\ntest_console.py\ntest_constrain.py\ntest_containers.py\ntest_control.py\ntest_emoji.py\ntest_file_proxy.py\ntest_filesize.py\ntest_getfileno.py\ntest_highlighter.py\ntest_inspect.py\ntest_json.py\ntest_jupyter.py\ntest_layout.py\ntest_live.py\ntest_live_render.py\ntest_log.py\ntest_logging.py\ntest_markdown.py\ntest_markdown_no_hyperlinks.py\ntest_markup.py\ntest_measure.py\ntest_null_file.py\ntest_padding.py\ntest_palette.py\ntest_panel.py\ntest_pick.py\ntest_pretty.py\ntest_progress.py\ntest_prompt.py\ntest_protocol.py\ntest_ratio.py\ntest_repr.py\ntest_rich_print.py\ntest_rule.py\ntest_rule_in_table.py\ntest_screen.py\ntest_segment.py\ntest_spinner.py\ntest_stack.py\ntest_status.py\ntest_style.py\ntest_styled.py\ntest_syntax.py\ntest_table.py\ntest_text.py\ntest_theme.py\ntest_tools.py\ntest_traceback.py\ntest_tree.py\ntest_unicode_data.py\ntest_win32_console.py\ntest_windows_renderer.py\n"}],"details":{}}}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"toolu_01HVrtp7Xy674bMNfqv8HAnK","toolName":"bash","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n----\n# ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nTerminal emulators operate on streams of characters interspersed with ANSI escape codes for styling and cursor movement. Without a unified primitive abstraction, high-level components (tables, syntax, markdown) would have to manually track escape codes, calculate visual cell widths, and handle cross-platform line breaks, leading to exponential complexity and bugs.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Atomic Segment Primitive:**  \n   Every visual element in Rich must ultimately reduce to a stream of `Segment` instances:\n   ```python\n   class Segment(NamedTuple):\n       text: str\n       style: Optional[Style] = None\n       control: Optional[Sequence[ControlCode]] = None\n   ```\n2. **Strict Invariants:**\n   - A `Segment` text piece must not contain unescaped newline characters `\\n` or `\\r` unless processed by `Segment.split_lines()` or `Segment.split_and_crop_lines()`.\n   - Visual measurement is derived strictly from `cell_len(segment.text)` using East Asian Width Unicode tables, never raw `len(text)`.\n   - Control sequences (cursor up, color palette queries) are encapsulated in the optional `control` field and take zero visual cell length.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- All rendering operations are stateless stream-processing pipelines.\n- Layout algorithms only need to measure and slice `Segment` collections.\n- Clean separation between logical layout calculation and physical terminal escape emission.\n----\n3:import os\n4:from typing import IO, TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable, Optional, Union\n6:from ._extension import load_ipython_extension  # noqa: F401\n8:__all__ = [\"get_console\", \"reconfigure\", \"print\", \"inspect\", \"print_json\"]\n----\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, List, Optional, Tuple, Union\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import (\n        Console,\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\n_card_render.py\nconftest.py\npytest.ini\nrender.py\ntest_align.py\ntest_ansi.py\ntest_bar.py\ntest_block_bar.py\ntest_box.py\ntest_card.py\ntest_cells.py\ntest_color.py\ntest_color_triplet.py\ntest_columns.py\ntest_columns_align.py\ntest_console.py\ntest_constrain.py\ntest_containers.py\ntest_control.py\ntest_emoji.py\ntest_file_proxy.py\ntest_filesize.py\ntest_getfileno.py\ntest_highlighter.py\ntest_inspect.py\ntest_json.py\ntest_jupyter.py\ntest_layout.py\ntest_live.py\ntest_live_render.py\ntest_log.py\ntest_logging.py\ntest_markdown.py\ntest_markdown_no_hyperlinks.py\ntest_markup.py\ntest_measure.py\ntest_null_file.py\ntest_padding.py\ntest_palette.py\ntest_panel.py\ntest_pick.py\ntest_pretty.py\ntest_progress.py\ntest_prompt.py\ntest_protocol.py\ntest_ratio.py\ntest_repr.py\ntest_rich_print.py\ntest_rule.py\ntest_rule_in_table.py\ntest_screen.py\ntest_segment.py\ntest_spinner.py\ntest_stack.py\ntest_status.py\ntest_style.py\ntest_styled.py\ntest_syntax.py\ntest_table.py\ntest_text.py\ntest_theme.py\ntest_tools.py\ntest_traceback.py\ntest_tree.py\ntest_unicode_data.py\ntest_win32_console.py\ntest_windows_renderer.py\n"}],"structuredContent":{"output":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n----\n# ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nTerminal emulators operate on streams of characters interspersed with ANSI escape codes for styling and cursor movement. Without a unified primitive abstraction, high-level components (tables, syntax, markdown) would have to manually track escape codes, calculate visual cell widths, and handle cross-platform line breaks, leading to exponential complexity and bugs.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Atomic Segment Primitive:**  \n   Every visual element in Rich must ultimately reduce to a stream of `Segment` instances:\n   ```python\n   class Segment(NamedTuple):\n       text: str\n       style: Optional[Style] = None\n       control: Optional[Sequence[ControlCode]] = None\n   ```\n2. **Strict Invariants:**\n   - A `Segment` text piece must not contain unescaped newline characters `\\n` or `\\r` unless processed by `Segment.split_lines()` or `Segment.split_and_crop_lines()`.\n   - Visual measurement is derived strictly from `cell_len(segment.text)` using East Asian Width Unicode tables, never raw `len(text)`.\n   - Control sequences (cursor up, color palette queries) are encapsulated in the optional `control` field and take zero visual cell length.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- All rendering operations are stateless stream-processing pipelines.\n- Layout algorithms only need to measure and slice `Segment` collections.\n- Clean separation between logical layout calculation and physical terminal escape emission.\n----\n3:import os\n4:from typing import IO, TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable, Optional, Union\n6:from ._extension import load_ipython_extension  # noqa: F401\n8:__all__ = [\"get_console\", \"reconfigure\", \"print\", \"inspect\", \"print_json\"]\n----\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, List, Optional, Tuple, Union\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import (\n        Console,\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\n_card_render.py\nconftest.py\npytest.ini\nrender.py\ntest_align.py\ntest_ansi.py\ntest_bar.py\ntest_block_bar.py\ntest_box.py\ntest_card.py\ntest_cells.py\ntest_color.py\ntest_color_triplet.py\ntest_columns.py\ntest_columns_align.py\ntest_console.py\ntest_constrain.py\ntest_containers.py\ntest_control.py\ntest_emoji.py\ntest_file_proxy.py\ntest_filesize.py\ntest_getfileno.py\ntest_highlighter.py\ntest_inspect.py\ntest_json.py\ntest_jupyter.py\ntest_layout.py\ntest_live.py\ntest_live_render.py\ntest_log.py\ntest_logging.py\ntest_markdown.py\ntest_markdown_no_hyperlinks.py\ntest_markup.py\ntest_measure.py\ntest_null_file.py\ntest_padding.py\ntest_palette.py\ntest_panel.py\ntest_pick.py\ntest_pretty.py\ntest_progress.py\ntest_prompt.py\ntest_protocol.py\ntest_ratio.py\ntest_repr.py\ntest_rich_print.py\ntest_rule.py\ntest_rule_in_table.py\ntest_screen.py\ntest_segment.py\ntest_spinner.py\ntest_stack.py\ntest_status.py\ntest_style.py\ntest_styled.py\ntest_syntax.py\ntest_table.py\ntest_text.py\ntest_theme.py\ntest_tools.py\ntest_traceback.py\ntest_tree.py\ntest_unicode_data.py\ntest_win32_console.py\ntest_windows_renderer.py\n","truncated":false,"exit_code":0,"wall_time_seconds":0}},"isError":false,"durationMs":22}
{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01HVrtp7Xy674bMNfqv8HAnK","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n----\n# ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nTerminal emulators operate on streams of characters interspersed with ANSI escape codes for styling and cursor movement. Without a unified primitive abstraction, high-level components (tables, syntax, markdown) would have to manually track escape codes, calculate visual cell widths, and handle cross-platform line breaks, leading to exponential complexity and bugs.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Atomic Segment Primitive:**  \n   Every visual element in Rich must ultimately reduce to a stream of `Segment` instances:\n   ```python\n   class Segment(NamedTuple):\n       text: str\n       style: Optional[Style] = None\n       control: Optional[Sequence[ControlCode]] = None\n   ```\n2. **Strict Invariants:**\n   - A `Segment` text piece must not contain unescaped newline characters `\\n` or `\\r` unless processed by `Segment.split_lines()` or `Segment.split_and_crop_lines()`.\n   - Visual measurement is derived strictly from `cell_len(segment.text)` using East Asian Width Unicode tables, never raw `len(text)`.\n   - Control sequences (cursor up, color palette queries) are encapsulated in the optional `control` field and take zero visual cell length.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- All rendering operations are stateless stream-processing pipelines.\n- Layout algorithms only need to measure and slice `Segment` collections.\n- Clean separation between logical layout calculation and physical terminal escape emission.\n----\n3:import os\n4:from typing import IO, TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable, Optional, Union\n6:from ._extension import load_ipython_extension  # noqa: F401\n8:__all__ = [\"get_console\", \"reconfigure\", \"print\", \"inspect\", \"print_json\"]\n----\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, List, Optional, Tuple, Union\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import (\n        Console,\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\n_card_render.py\nconftest.py\npytest.ini\nrender.py\ntest_align.py\ntest_ansi.py\ntest_bar.py\ntest_block_bar.py\ntest_box.py\ntest_card.py\ntest_cells.py\ntest_color.py\ntest_color_triplet.py\ntest_columns.py\ntest_columns_align.py\ntest_console.py\ntest_constrain.py\ntest_containers.py\ntest_control.py\ntest_emoji.py\ntest_file_proxy.py\ntest_filesize.py\ntest_getfileno.py\ntest_highlighter.py\ntest_inspect.py\ntest_json.py\ntest_jupyter.py\ntest_layout.py\ntest_live.py\ntest_live_render.py\ntest_log.py\ntest_logging.py\ntest_markdown.py\ntest_markdown_no_hyperlinks.py\ntest_markup.py\ntest_measure.py\ntest_null_file.py\ntest_padding.py\ntest_palette.py\ntest_panel.py\ntest_pick.py\ntest_pretty.py\ntest_progress.py\ntest_prompt.py\ntest_protocol.py\ntest_ratio.py\ntest_repr.py\ntest_rich_print.py\ntest_rule.py\ntest_rule_in_table.py\ntest_screen.py\ntest_segment.py\ntest_spinner.py\ntest_stack.py\ntest_status.py\ntest_style.py\ntest_styled.py\ntest_syntax.py\ntest_table.py\ntest_text.py\ntest_theme.py\ntest_tools.py\ntest_traceback.py\ntest_tree.py\ntest_unicode_data.py\ntest_win32_console.py\ntest_windows_renderer.py\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":22,"timestamp":1794168274221}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01HVrtp7Xy674bMNfqv8HAnK","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n----\n# ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nTerminal emulators operate on streams of characters interspersed with ANSI escape codes for styling and cursor movement. Without a unified primitive abstraction, high-level components (tables, syntax, markdown) would have to manually track escape codes, calculate visual cell widths, and handle cross-platform line breaks, leading to exponential complexity and bugs.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Atomic Segment Primitive:**  \n   Every visual element in Rich must ultimately reduce to a stream of `Segment` instances:\n   ```python\n   class Segment(NamedTuple):\n       text: str\n       style: Optional[Style] = None\n       control: Optional[Sequence[ControlCode]] = None\n   ```\n2. **Strict Invariants:**\n   - A `Segment` text piece must not contain unescaped newline characters `\\n` or `\\r` unless processed by `Segment.split_lines()` or `Segment.split_and_crop_lines()`.\n   - Visual measurement is derived strictly from `cell_len(segment.text)` using East Asian Width Unicode tables, never raw `len(text)`.\n   - Control sequences (cursor up, color palette queries) are encapsulated in the optional `control` field and take zero visual cell length.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- All rendering operations are stateless stream-processing pipelines.\n- Layout algorithms only need to measure and slice `Segment` collections.\n- Clean separation between logical layout calculation and physical terminal escape emission.\n----\n3:import os\n4:from typing import IO, TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable, Optional, Union\n6:from ._extension import load_ipython_extension  # noqa: F401\n8:__all__ = [\"get_console\", \"reconfigure\", \"print\", \"inspect\", \"print_json\"]\n----\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, List, Optional, Tuple, Union\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import (\n        Console,\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\n_card_render.py\nconftest.py\npytest.ini\nrender.py\ntest_align.py\ntest_ansi.py\ntest_bar.py\ntest_block_bar.py\ntest_box.py\ntest_card.py\ntest_cells.py\ntest_color.py\ntest_color_triplet.py\ntest_columns.py\ntest_columns_align.py\ntest_console.py\ntest_constrain.py\ntest_containers.py\ntest_control.py\ntest_emoji.py\ntest_file_proxy.py\ntest_filesize.py\ntest_getfileno.py\ntest_highlighter.py\ntest_inspect.py\ntest_json.py\ntest_jupyter.py\ntest_layout.py\ntest_live.py\ntest_live_render.py\ntest_log.py\ntest_logging.py\ntest_markdown.py\ntest_markdown_no_hyperlinks.py\ntest_markup.py\ntest_measure.py\ntest_null_file.py\ntest_padding.py\ntest_palette.py\ntest_panel.py\ntest_pick.py\ntest_pretty.py\ntest_progress.py\ntest_prompt.py\ntest_protocol.py\ntest_ratio.py\ntest_repr.py\ntest_rich_print.py\ntest_rule.py\ntest_rule_in_table.py\ntest_screen.py\ntest_segment.py\ntest_spinner.py\ntest_stack.py\ntest_status.py\ntest_style.py\ntest_styled.py\ntest_syntax.py\ntest_table.py\ntest_text.py\ntest_theme.py\ntest_tools.py\ntest_traceback.py\ntest_tree.py\ntest_unicode_data.py\ntest_win32_console.py\ntest_windows_renderer.py\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":22,"timestamp":1794168274221}}
